is_Meadow_and_Wood_6.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Glamis_Meadow_and_Wood_6.jpg/500px-Glamis_Meadow_and_Wood_6.jpg","caption":"Glamis Meadow and Wood","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glamis_Meadow_and_Wood_6.jpg","ok_print":false}],"intro":{"body":"Wellingborough is a market town and borough in Northamptonshire, England, situated some 11 miles (18 km) from the county town of Northampton. The town is situated on the north side of the River Nene (pronounced Nenn in these parts), most of the older town is sited on the flanks of the hills above the river's current flood plain. Due to frequent flooding by the River Nene, the town was mostly built above the current level of the flood plain. Originally named \"Wendelingburgh\", the town was founded in the early 6th century Saxon period by a Saxon leader called Waendel and is mentioned in the Domesday Book under the name of \"Wendelburie\".","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Wellingborough","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Wellingborough","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Wellingborough is a historic market town in Northamptonshire, in the United Kingdom, with close to fifty seven thousand people. Finedon Hall and Hinwick House lead the sights, across a full nine hours. June through September are the best months.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":56564,"visit_h":9}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-the-castle","name":"The Castle","kind":"Theatre","lat":52.30008,"lon":-0.68806,"dist_km":0.5,"sig":1.118,"rank_score":5.1,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-wellingborough-station","name":"Wellingborough station","kind":"Landmark","lat":52.30384,"lon":-0.6766,"dist_km":1.2,"sig":2.483,"rank_score":4.3,"resolved_by":"retyped","fact":"Railway station in Northamptonshire, England","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Wellingboroughstationbuilding.jpg/960px-Wellingboroughstationbuilding.jpg","page":"https://commons.wik